    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with a high-ceiling core, led by **Corbin Carroll** (82.13) and **Mickey Moniak** (75.98). **Corbin Carroll** is our premier play, benefiting from a favorable matchup against Michael McGreevy and a significant boost from his projected #3 spot in the order. Similarly, **Mickey Moniak** is in a prime position to capitalize on a +14% park factor and an excellent matchup against Singer, whose xERA of 4.47 allows **Mickey Moniak** to project as an elite play. **Seiya Suzuki** (75.03) rounds out the top tier, bolstered by a 19% SP skill advantage against Ober and favorable wind conditions that further elevate his output potential.\n\nThe most difficult decision on today\u2019s card was leaving **Josh Naylor** (58.11) on the bench. He was the strongest performer outside the active roster, but his value was suppressed by a poor park factor and a neutralized matchup against Roupp. The optimizer favored **Kyle Karros** (59.51) in the 3B slot, largely due to the massive 14% park adjustment in his favor. We are also monitoring a 30% rain risk for **Austin Riley** (66.75); while his projected score is high, the weather risk combined with a potential late-game disruption keeps his volatility higher than that of our other starters.\n\nBeyond the core, we are leaning heavily on favorable platoon splits and park environments to maintain our edge in this 5x5 Roto format. **Vinnie Pasquantino** (71.77) sees a massive 14% boost from his platoon advantage against King, making him a cornerstone for runs and RBI production. Meanwhile, we remain cautious regarding the \"Lineup Pending\" tags for **Gabriel Moreno** and **James Wood**. While **James Wood** possesses elite xwOBA metrics, his score is tempered by an elite catcher matchup and a high stolen-base-hold rate from the opposition, which mitigates his immediate SB upside today. We will keep a close watch on these lineups to ensure the projected order advantages for **Gabriel Moreno** and **James Wood** hold firm.",
